  "output": "Here's the full performance analysis with actionable code examples:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n\n#### 1.1 Sequential DB queries in realtime-plugin.ts (HIGH)\n**`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts:63-143`** — Inside `Post` and `Comment` mutation handlers, `db.group.findUnique()` and `db.post.findUnique()` fire per row inside a loop.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Current: N queries for N posts\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const group = await db.group.findUnique({ where: { id: row.groupId } })\n  // ...per-row work\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: batch-load before the loop\nconst groupIds = [...new Set(rows.map(r => r.groupId))]\nconst groups = await db.group.findMany({ where: { id: { in: groupIds } } })\nconst groupMap = new Map(groups.map(g => [g.id, g]))\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const group = groupMap.get(row.groupId)\n}\n```\n\n#### 1.2 GroupMember handler — nested queries per member (HIGH)\n**`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts:231-288`** — `db.group.findUnique()` is called inside a `for` loop, plus admin/notification queries per member.\n\n```ts\n// ❌ Current\nfor (const member of memberRows) {\n  const group = await db.group.findUnique(...)  // called N times\n  await notify(...)\n}\n\n// ✅ Fix: lift lookup outside the loop\nconst group = await db.group.findUnique({ where: { id: memberRows[0].groupId } })\nawait Promise.all(memberRows.map(member => notify(group, member)))\n```\n\n#### 1.3 `conversationMemberIds()` called multiple times per message event (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts:52-59, 292-354`** — The same member list is queried 2–3 times per message mutation.\n\n```ts\n// ✅ Fix: cache within the handler scope using a Map\nconst memberCache = new Map<string, string[]>()\nasync function getMembers(convId: string) {\n  if (!memberCache.has(convId)) {\n    const rows = await db.conversationMember.findMany({ where: { conversationId: convId } })\n    memberCache.set(convId, rows.map(r => r.userId))\n  }\n  return memberCache.get(convId)!\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Unnecessary Re-renders\n\n#### 2.1 Comment thread O(n²) filtering on every render (HIGH)\n**`apps/web/src/components/feed/comments-thread.tsx:58-83`** — `repliesOf` creates a new function and iterates all comments on every render.\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Current\nconst top = (comments ?? []).filter((c) => !c.parentId)\nconst repliesOf = (id: string) => (comments ?? []).filter((c) => c.parentId === id)\n\n// ✅ Fix\nconst { top, repliesMap } = useMemo(() => {\n  const top: Comment[] = []\n  const repliesMap = new Map<string, Comment[]>()\n  for (const c of comments ?? []) {\n    if (!c.parentId) top.push(c)\n    else {\n      const bucket = repliesMap.get(c.parentId) ?? []\n      bucket.push(c)\n      repliesMap.set(c.parentId, bucket)\n    }\n  }\n  return { top, repliesMap }\n}, [comments])\nconst repliesOf = useCallback((id: string) => repliesMap.get(id) ?? [], [repliesMap])\n```\n\n#### 2.2 Conversation list: title computation + filter on every render (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/conversation-list.tsx:50-66`**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Current — new array every render, O(n) string ops every keystroke\nconst rows = (data ?? []).map((item) => ({ item, title: conversationTitle(...) }))\nconst filtered = term ? rows.filter(({ title }) => title.toLowerCase().includes(term)) : rows\n\n// ✅ Fix\nconst rows = useMemo(\n  () => (data ?? []).map((item) => ({ item, title: conversationTitle(item.conversation, item.conversation.members, me.id) })),\n  [data, me.id]\n)\nconst filtered = useMemo(\n  () => term ? rows.filter(({ title }) => title.toLowerCase().includes(term)) : rows,\n  [rows, term]\n)\n```\n\n#### 2.3 Contacts rail — sort on every render (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/web/src/components/layout/contacts-rail.tsx:26-28`**\n\n```tsx\n// ❌ Current\nconst sorted = [...people].sort((a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id)))\n\n// ✅ Fix\nconst sorted = useMemo(\n  () => [...people].sort((a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id))),\n  [people, online]\n)\n```\n\n#### 2.4 Presence context re-renders entire subtree (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/web/src/hooks/use-presence.tsx:7-21`** — Every online/offline event triggers a context update that re-renders all subscribers (sidebar, feed avatars, chat list).\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ Fix: expose a selector hook instead of raw context\nconst OnlineContext = createContext<Set<string>>(new Set())\nexport const useIsOnline = (userId: string) => {\n  const online = useContext(OnlineContext)\n  return online.has(userId)\n}\n// Components subscribe only to their own user's status, not the full set\n```\n\n#### 2.5 Missing `React.memo` on `MessageRow` (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:201-240`** — New message arriving causes all existing rows to re-render because `actions` is an inline object.\n\n```tsx\n// ✅ Fix\nconst MessageRow = memo(function MessageRow({ message, actions, ...props }) {\n  // ...\n})\n\n// In parent — memoize the actions object\nconst actions = useMemo(() => ({ onJumpTo: jumpTo, onReact, onDelete }), [jumpTo, onReact, onDelete])\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n#### 3.1 Conversation list invalidated on every message (HIGH)\n**`apps/web/src/hooks/use-realtime-sync.ts`** — `message:new` invalidates `[\"conversation\"]` causing a full list refetch on each message.\n\n```ts\n// ✅ Fix: update the specific conversation's lastMessageAt in cache optimistically\n// instead of invalidating the whole list\nuseSocketEvent(\"message:new\", (msg) => {\n  qc.setQueryData([\"conversationMember\", \"findMany\", ...], (old) =>\n    old?.map(item =>\n      item.conversationId === msg.conversationId\n        ? { ...item, conversation: { ...item.conversation, lastMessageAt: msg.createdAt } }\n        : item\n    )\n  )\n})\n```\n\n#### 3.2 Post reaction invalidates entire feed (MEDIUM)\n**`apps/web/src/components/feed/post-card.tsx:94`** — `invalidates: [\"postReaction\", \"post\"]` refetches all posts when one reaction changes.\n\n```ts\n// ✅ Fix: optimistic update + targeted invalidation\nconst { mutate } = useDbMutation(\"postReaction\", \"upsert\", {\n  onMutate: async ({ where, create }) => {\n    await qc.cancelQueries({ queryKey: [\"post\", postId] })\n    const prev = qc.getQueryData([\"post\", postId])\n    qc.setQueryData([\"post\", postId], (old) => ({\n      ...old,\n      reactions: [...old.reactions, create],\n    }))\n    return { prev }\n  },\n  onError: (_, __, ctx) => qc.setQueryData([\"post\", postId], ctx?.prev),\n  onSettled: () => qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"post\", postId] }),\n})\n```\n\n#### 3.3 Static data (org, groups) has no extended staleTime (LOW)\n**`apps/web/src/lib/query.ts:24-36`** — Add model-specific overrides.\n\n```ts\nconst STALE_TIMES: Partial<Record<string, number>> = {\n  organization: 10 * 60_000,\n  groupMember: 5 * 60_000,\n  user: 5 * 60_000,\n}\n// Use in useDbQuery via the model name\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n#### 4.1 WebSocket hub Maps grow unbounded (CRITICAL)\n**`apps/api/src/websocket/hub.ts:27-215`** — `connOwner` and room member Sets are cleaned on disconnect, but ghost entries can accumulate after thousands of connections over long deployments. Add a periodic audit:\n\n```ts\n// Run every 30 minutes — remove rooms with no active connections\nsetInterval(() => {\n  for (const [room, conns] of members) {\n    if (conns.size === 0) members.delete(room)\n  }\n}, 30 * 60_000)\n```\n\n#### 4.2 `answered` Set in calls.ts never trimmed (HIGH)\n**`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:25`** — The `answered` Set tracks call IDs forever. Add cleanup when a call ends:\n\n```ts\nfunction endCall(callId: string) {\n  live.delete(callId)\n  answered.delete(callId)  // ensure this runs in ALL exit paths\n}\n```\n\n#### 4.3 Request ID counter can overflow in realtime.ts (LOW)\n**`apps/web/src/lib/realtime.ts:41`** — After 2^53 requests the counter silently wraps. Trivially fixed:\n\n```ts\nthis.nextReqId = (this.nextReqId + 1) % Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Priority Checklist\n\n| Priority | Issue | File | Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🔴 CRITICAL | Hub Map unbounded growth | `websocket/hub.ts` | Server OOM |\n| 🔴 HIGH | N+1 in realtime-plugin loops | `server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts` | DB overload |\n| 🔴 HIGH | Conversation list full refetch on message | `hooks/use-realtime-sync.ts` | Network storm |\n| 🟠 HIGH | Comment O(n²) filtering | `components/feed/comments-thread.tsx` | UI jank |\n| 🟠 HIGH | `answered` Set unbounded | `websocket/calls.ts` | Memory leak |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | Missing `useMemo` on conversation rows/filter | `chat/conversation-list.tsx` | Keystroke lag |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | Presence context full-tree re-render | `hooks/use-presence.tsx` | Sidebar flicker |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | `MessageRow` not memoized | `chat/message-list.tsx` | Chat jank |\n| 🟡 MEDIUM | Reaction invalidates all posts | `feed/post-card.tsx` | Feed flicker |\n| 🟢 LOW | Contacts sort not memoized | `layout/contacts-rail.tsx` | Minor lag |\n\nThe two highest-leverage fixes are: **batching the realtime-plugin DB queries** (eliminates the biggest server-side scaling bottleneck) and **switching `message:new` from cache invalidation to optimistic updates** (eliminates the most frequent unnecessary network round-trips).\n",
